Good morning,

We are instructed to notify water damage to a third party's building on behalf of our client Tidewater Roofing & Exteriors, LLC. Our reference is CB/ROOF/2024/3376. This is within the 48-hour requirement for water intrusion into a building our client has worked on.

Policy number: GL-3376-90284
Insured name: Tidewater Roofing & Exteriors, LLC
Contract number: SCPS-2025-RF-011
Date of loss: 18 June 2025
Loss location: 4652 Driver Lane, Suffolk, VA 23435
Cause: Rain into a roof left open during tear-off
Estimated loss: USD 510,000

Our client is part way through a phased TPO re-roof at Driver Middle School under
a summer-recess contract with Suffolk City Public Schools, who are a scheduled
certificate holder on the policy.

They tore off about 9,400 sq ft on Wednesday and had 6,200 sq ft dried in when a
fast-developing cell arrived about ninety minutes early. Water came in over the
3,200 sq ft that had not been reached, into eight classrooms and the media centre.

There was no hot work - it is a mechanically fastened system - and no
subcontractors; all labour was our client's own W-2 crew. The morning forecast
check, the tear-off photographs and the dry-in photographs are all retained and
are with the consultant's report.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * roofing consultant's report
  * reinstatement schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. The division has referenced
liquidated damages under the construction contract; our client's position is that
those are contractual and are not tendered as an insured loss.

